task: native-interpreter-allocation (measurement: is bindChain's 2-3x on Native the collector or the mutator?)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-06
branch: feature/native-interpreter-allocation

why: §18 has bindChain at 497-517 us on Native against ~190 JVM / 164-230
  JS, same code path, and the entry asks for a Native allocation profile
  before anything is changed. The instrument exists: Scala Native 0.5's
  immix GC writes one row per collection (mark/nullify/sweep ns) to the
  file named by GC_STATS_FILE, and GC_INITIAL_HEAP_SIZE fixes the heap.
  Two runs of the one lane answer the question: default heap with the
  stats file (how much of the wall time is the collector), and a heap
  large enough that nothing is collected (what bindChain costs with the
  collector out of the picture). BenchCross gains a BENCH_LANES env
  filter so one lane owns the stats file; nothing else changes unless
  the numbers say the mutator is the cost, in which case the closure
  count per step is the next entry, not this one.
